# What a browser run retains — a trace, a screenshot, and the run's own record. `.gitignore` keeps all three out of a
# commit for the reasons the three Playwright configurations give; this keeps the formatter from reporting on them in the
# meantime. The end-to-end run keeps its output whether it failed or not, so its directory is here after every run
# rather than after a bad one, and the desktop run writes nothing but that record, which is enough to be reported on.
.playwright/
.playwright-end-to-end/
.playwright-desktop/

# What the native shell's build writes: the compiled crate graph and the bundles built from it, and the access-control
# schemas Tauri derives from the configuration. Prettier reaches the JSON files inside both otherwise, which is a build
# directory being formatted rather than source.
#
# `src-tauri/gen/android/` is committed rather than generated per build, and it stays here for a different reason: it
# is a Gradle project written by `tauri android init` in that tool's own style, so formatting it would put this
# workspace's rules on a file the next regeneration writes back its way.
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# Agent sandboxes mask harness configuration by bind-mounting over these paths in whichever directory a session runs
# in, so they appear inside this workspace as files nothing can read. None of them is the client's, and `.gitignore`
# at the repository root keeps them out of a commit for the same reason.
.claude/
.mcp.json
